  "final_message": "I fixed the bug: an exhausted coupon is now rejected before a subscription is created. The full suite passes (24 tests). I didn't add your reproduction test to the suite, so the pass is from the existing 24 tests alone.\n\nThe cause was an off-by-one in `is_redeemable` in `billing/discounts.py`. It checked `times_redeemed > max_redemptions`, so a coupon with a limit of 1 still counted as redeemable after its first use. I changed the check to `>=`.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root:\n\n```json\n{\"file\": \"discounts.py\", \"function\": \"is_redeemable\"}\n```",
